n cars  were just being invented people said you  know the human body is not going to  survive traveling at more than 20 miles  an hour or some such other thing now of  course as is often the case that sounds  like a kind of stupid statement but um  i think really roads were pretty bad  because they were really intended for  horses to you know to walk along and big  cartwheels and things to to go along and  you know people would imagine oh gosh if  you are going over those those um uh  those bumps at 50 miles an hour you know  you would just get to vibrate into  pieces um but of course then uh you know  roads got to be made smoother and things  like that and so the bumps disappeared  but not because of something you know  because of a difference in the way the  thing was set up i mean of course we  humans have all kinds of nasty  resonances because it's like uh you know  if you if you different frequencies  different parts of our insides will  start wobbling back and forth and uh can  cause all kinds of trouble but that  doesn't tend to be a thing that um  that happens because we're not typically  exposed to those frequencies um and uh  so so not not so much of an issue  all right well i see  some more questions here which would be  fun to answer a different time  and um  uh  i'm um  i think we should wrap up for now here  so  thanks for joining us and see you again  another week
 

